        "evidence": "The block is two sentences. The first states an axiom ('The Hopf comultiplication Delta_q on O_q(SU(2)) obeys coassociativity'); the second - 'This property is required for consistency across the theoretical framework.' - is placed purely to end the block and carries no content. It names no consistency condition, no result that depends on coassociativity, and no framework component; it would remain equally true and equally empty attached to any axiom in the corpus. Coassociativity is part of the DEFINITION of a Hopf algebra, so 'required for consistency' is not even a claim about this object.",
